    "realname": "Paul Leighton Johnson",
    "profile": "American house DJ and producer\r\nBorn: 11th January 1971 Chicago, IL - died: 4th August 2021 Chicago, IL.\r\nHe released a vast amount of music for some of the most consistently underground dance labels before hooking up with [l=Peacefrog Records]. 12\" releases on the likes of [l=Cajual Records] / [l=Relief Records] and [l=Dance Mania] led to his debut album release \"Bump Talkin'\" in 1996. This and the follow up \"Feel The Music\" became two of the most talked about releases of their time.\r\nHe lost the use of his legs as a result of a shooting accident in 1987, and required a wheelchair for mobility.\r\nCo-founded [l=Dust Traxx, Inc.] in 1997 and ran his own label [l=Nocturnal Interludes].",
